  "declared_implementation_notes": [
    "refusal set: the outside refusal value is max(U_work, U_neither). PRE_DECLARATIONS.md sec.2.4 also lists U_both; U_both is the frozen block's school+work state and, used as an outside value, would let a cell collect the schooling value plus child earnings without occupying a place. The count of cells on which U_both would have dominated Tier O is reported per country-year-level in column both_would_dominate_cells.",
    "outside option evaluated at each lattice cell's own income y_i (the four-state block's equations and parameters are unchanged; only the income argument is the cell's rather than the representative household's).",
    "tertiary: the frozen child block is undefined at L=3 (AGE_W and cost_base each have 3 entries), so the tertiary tier composition inherits the same-year upper-secondary choice shares while the aggregate stays the model's own tertiary demand.",
    "D_O is evaluated at the open tier's gate state (R_O=1, V_O=0, dpi=0), the v1.3 g0 no-gate control that sec.9 uses as the (c-i) baseline; it is therefore year-invariant and country-specific.",
    "the kappa cap acts on the official-age entry cohort and, at upper secondary, reduces admission in the order over-age -> Tier H -> Tier O, so the unfilled-Tier-O object is never manufactured by the cap (reported in kappa_cap_audit.csv)."
  ],
